cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use OraCalm, please cite this software AND the original instrument(s) you used."
title: "OraCalm: open, multilingual scoring for validated dental-anxiety instruments"
abstract: >-
  OraCalm is a dependency-free Python library, command-line tool, and web demo
  that scores widely used, validated dental-anxiety instruments (MDAS, Corah's
  DAS, and the faces version of the MCDAS), applying their published cut-offs
  and interpretation bands with full source attribution and multilingual item
  sets. It is an educational/research aid, not a diagnostic device.
type: software
